## 2. Tech Stack — Final Decisions

| Layer | Technology | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **Framework** | Next.js 14+ (App Router, TypeScript) | SSR, API routes, file-based routing — everything in one project |
| **Database** | Supabase PostgreSQL | Managed Postgres, free tier = 500MB (sufficient for MVP), no DevOps |
| **ORM** | Prisma | Type-safe queries, migration management, schema-as-code |
| **Auth** | Supabase Auth (Email OTP + password) | Built-in email OTP, session management, JWT — no SMS provider needed |
| **Storage** | Supabase Storage | Signature images, CNIC photos, generated PDFs — 1GB free |
| **E-Signature** | `signature_pad` (MIT, client-side) | No external API dependency; audit trail built around it |
| **PDF Generation** | Puppeteer (`puppeteer-core` + `@sparticuz/chromium`) | HTML/CSS → PDF gives full design control for professional contracts |
| **Email** | Resend | OTP delivery, notifications, reminders, signed PDF attachment — 100 emails/day free |
| **Hashing** | Node.js `crypto` (SHA-256) | Built-in, no dependency — for document integrity verification |
| **Device Fingerprint** | `@fingerprintjs/fingerprintjs` (open-source) | Client-side device identification for audit trail |
| **Styling** | Vanilla CSS with CSS custom properties | Full control, no framework overhead |
| **Fonts** | Google Fonts (Inter) | Clean, professional, modern typography |
| **Deployment** | Vercel (app) + Supabase Cloud (backend) | Zero-config Next.js deployment, free tiers for both |

### What We're NOT Using (and Why)

| Skipped | Reason |
|---|---|
| Twilio / SMS / WhatsApp | Email-only for MVP — eliminates cost, WhatsApp verification delay, and SMS per-message fees |
| Redis / BullMQ | No background job queue needed at MVP volume |
| Full RBAC library | Simple `role` field (creator/brand/agency) is sufficient |
| AI layer | Deferred entirely |
| Sentry / OpenTelemetry | Basic `console.error` + Vercel logs is enough for now |
| Native mobile apps | Post-PMF |
| Payment processing | Platform is free for now |

