## 6. Authentication — Email OTP Only

### 6.1 Sign-Up Flow (Creator / Brand / Agency)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor U as User
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as API Route
    participant SA as Supabase Auth
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    U->>FE: Fill sign-up form<br/>(name, email, phone, role, password)
    FE->>API: POST /api/auth/signup
    API->>SA: supabase.auth.signUp({email, password})
    SA-->>U: Sends OTP to email (magic code)
    U->>FE: Enter 6-digit OTP from email
    FE->>API: POST /api/auth/verify-otp
    API->>SA: supabase.auth.verifyOtp({email, token, type: 'email'})
    SA-->>API: Session + JWT
    API->>DB: INSERT into users (name, email, phone, role, supabase_auth_id)
    API-->>FE: Redirect to dashboard
```

### 6.2 Respondent OTP (No Account — Public Link)

When a brand or creator receives a contract link and needs to verify identity before signing:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor R as Respondent
    participant FE as Public Contract Page
    participant API as API Route
    participant RE as Resend

    R->>FE: Fill respondent fields on contract
    R->>FE: Enter email address
    FE->>API: POST /api/contracts/share/:token/send-otp
    API->>API: Generate 6-digit OTP, store with 10-min expiry
    API->>RE: Send email with OTP code
    RE-->>R: Email with 6-digit code
    R->>FE: Enter OTP
    FE->>API: POST /api/contracts/share/:token/verify-otp
    API->>API: Validate OTP matches + not expired
    API-->>FE: OTP verified, enable signature pad
    R->>FE: Draw signature + click "I Agree"
    FE->>API: POST /api/contracts/share/:token/sign
    API-->>FE: Signature recorded
```

> [!NOTE]
> For respondent-side OTP (without a Supabase account), we use a **simple OTP table** or in-memory store:
> ```prisma
> model OtpVerification {
>   id        String   @id @default(uuid())
>   email     String
>   code      String   // 6-digit code
>   expiresAt DateTime @map("expires_at")
>   verified  Boolean  @default(false)
>   attempts  Int      @default(0) // max 5 attempts
>   createdAt DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at")
>   @@map("otp_verifications")
> }
> ```

