## 9. E-Signature Implementation

### Architecture (unchanged from v1, but OTP is now email-based)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor S as Signer
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant FP as FingerprintJS
    participant API as API Route
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant ST as Supabase Storage

    S->>FE: Click "Sign Contract"
    FE->>FE: Show SignatureModal
    FE->>FP: Get device fingerprint
    FP-->>FE: Fingerprint hash
    S->>FE: Draw signature on canvas
    S->>FE: Check "I have read and agree to all terms"
    S->>FE: Click "Sign & Submit"
    FE->>FE: signaturePad.toDataURL() → base64 PNG
    FE->>FE: Compute SHA-256 of displayed contract content
    FE->>API: POST /sign {signature_b64, doc_hash, fingerprint, consent: true}
    API->>API: Capture server timestamp, IP, user-agent
    API->>API: Verify email OTP was completed for this session
    API->>ST: Upload signature PNG
    ST-->>API: Signature URL
    API->>DB: INSERT into signatures (all metadata)
    API->>DB: INSERT into audit_logs
    API->>DB: UPDATE contract status
    API-->>FE: Signature recorded
```

### Metadata Captured Per Signature

| Field | Source | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `signed_at` | Server clock (`new Date()`) | Tamper-proof timestamp |
| `ip_address` | `req.headers['x-forwarded-for']` | Geo/identity correlation |
| `user_agent` | `req.headers['user-agent']` | Device/browser identification |
| `device_fingerprint` | FingerprintJS (client) | Additional device identity |
| `document_hash` | SHA-256 of contract JSON at signing time | Proves exactly what was agreed to |
| `otp_verified` | Server session state | Confirms identity was verified |
| `otp_email` | From OTP verification step | Links signature to a verified email |
| `consent_recorded` | Explicit checkbox + button click | Legal "meeting of minds" evidence |
| `signature_image_url` | Canvas → PNG → Supabase Storage | Visual representation |

