## 12. Security Measures

| Concern | Solution |
|---|---|
| **OTP brute force** | Max 5 attempts per email per 15 minutes; OTP expires after 10 minutes |
| **Share link guessing** | UUID v4 tokens (122 bits of entropy — unguessable) |
| **Contract tampering** | SHA-256 hash computed at signing + stored; any change detectable |
| **CNIC data protection** | Private Supabase Storage bucket; RLS policies restrict access to owner only |
| **Signature image security** | Private storage bucket; served via signed URLs with expiry |
| **CSRF** | Next.js built-in CSRF protection on server actions |
| **XSS** | React's default escaping + CSP headers |
| **SQL injection** | Prisma parameterized queries (no raw SQL) |
| **Session hijacking** | Supabase Auth with httpOnly cookies, secure flag |
| **Audit trail immutability** | Audit log table: INSERT-only (no UPDATE/DELETE permissions via RLS) |
| **Email OTP spam** | Rate limit: max 3 OTP requests per email per hour |

